1.1, R1.2, R1.4, R1.5. R1.3 is absent from source_code but likely maps to a mage build target (magefiles/ is excluded by DD7). The only code generation target from prd011 is cmd/version, which exists.\n- **uc002-format:** pkg/format implements prd003-format R1 (column alignment), R2 (ANSI color with TTY detection), R3 (human-readable sizes). All sub-requirements are annotated and tested.\n- **uc003-sys:** pkg/sys implements prd002-sys R1 (terminal size via TIOCGWINSZ) and R2 (extended file metadata via Lstat with platform-specific extraction). The package doc claims full coverage of R1 and R2. Architecture-listed capabilities beyond R1/R2 (signal handling, process groups, process priority) are annotated for specific later utilities and are not anchored to current PRD requirements.\n- **uc004-testutils:** pkg/testutils implements prd001-testutils R1–R5 comprehensively: DiffTest struct (R1), binary execution with timeout (R2), byte-level comparison of stdout/stderr/exit code (R3), timestamp and composable normalizers (R4), and file-state verification (R5).\n\nThe analysis confirms `gaps: []` — no consistency errors or missing coverage. All PRD requirements referenced in source_code have corresponding implementations and tests.\n\n## Proposed Tasks\n\nNo code generation tasks remain for release 00.0. All foundational packages exist in source_code with both implementation and test coverage matching the PRD requirements referenced in the code. The architecture's extended capabilities (signal handling, process groups, process priority, Stat function) are scoped to later utilities and cannot be anchored to verified PRD requirement IDs without access to the PRD text.\n\n```yaml\n[]\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":47314,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":47314},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_availa